title ALES171 — Lotus's stereo_shelf: the two-band bass-and-treble tone shelf carried into stereo, the SAME coefficient and band gains on BOTH channels — the second rung of the stereo EQ / filter class
prompt Autonomous loop lap after ALES170: take the next agent-doable crux Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61 as its own signed round, STOP at custody gates.
think ALES170 opened the stereo EQ class with the tone control, which only REMOVES a band. The natural second rung is the two-band shelf (mono ALES41) — bass and treble knobs, the everyday equalizer — carried into stereo. Same parametric pattern as ALES170 and ALES130: the coefficient and band gains are fractions the caller names, not measured scalars, so the SAME knobs on both channels preserve the image for free.
think Simpler than ALES170: ALES41's shelf runs a fresh low-pass over the whole span each call, so there is NO carried state to thread across a seam — a stereo shelf is a stateless per-channel pass. Composed it as: StereoShelfError = shelf.ShelfError reused whole; validate coeff + both band gains + span once against the shared length before either channel writes (atomic refusal), then shelf.shelf on each channel with the same params.
think Proved four laws against the real ALES41 tool: stereo shelf law (each channel == mono shelf byte for byte, channels genuinely differing); flat-EQ identity law (unity on both bands the identity on both — the bands reconstruct L+(x-L)=x — bass doubling a settled constant while treble leaves it, the knobs orthogonal at DC); image law (identical-channel master stays identical, same knobs same content same output); balance/silence/atomicity/degenerate (five refusals each leaving both channels untouched and balanced).
obs No custody gate reached — pure local i16 DSP siloed to lotus/, a self-approved design round. Built and ran on metal; witness GREEN through Rishi, TAME clean (opening triad, ≥2 asserts/fn with // invariant, no @memcpy, named errors with try, i64 scale-then-clamp-once per ALES8's fader lesson inherited from ALES41). Second EQ rung landed after ALES170 opened the class.
loom witness=ales_stereo_shelf_witness selftest=GREEN laws=4 channels=2 class=eq-filter-rung-2
